# Non-canonical binary naturals in lambda plus merge: problems of the
# reduction series that are A DOMAIN TRAP IN THE REDUCTION SERIES.
#
# A binary natural is canonical when no even has zero as its half
# (lambda_jit_scott_decoding:binary_tree/2); `even zero` is another term
# with the value 0, and Scott case analysis tells the two apart. The
# definitional plus of contest_merge_dynamic.pl keeps such forms: a sum
# with zero answers the other operand as it is, and an even plus an even
# is the even of the halves' sum, so `plus (even zero) zero` is
# `even zero`, not `zero`, and leading even-over-zero digits of an operand
# stay in the sum. The answer of each problem is that tree, computed by a
# reference that follows the definitional code case by case
# (plus_tree/3), not by the value.
#
# THE TRAP: a knowledge base or replacement that plants the canonical
# literal of the sum's VALUE gives a term that decodes to another tree, so
# the judge's decoding reads a wrong answer, a false positive under rule
# 30. Rule 35's condition, that a replacement is a head beta equal to the
# definitional code's, is what such a layer breaks here: the canonical
# literal and the non-canonical sum have one value and are not beta equal.
#
# THE PROBLEMS:
# - reduction_non_canonical_even_zero: plus (even zero) zero, the answer
#   even zero;
# - reduction_non_canonical_sum_N_digits, N = 16, 32 and 64: the sum of
#   the two factors of contest_merge_binary.pl's product of N digits, the
#   left written with eight leading even-over-zero digits and the right
#   with four; the answers keep six, seven and five leading
#   even-over-zero digits (the longer operand's bits and the carries
#   cover the rest).
#
# READINGS (2026-09-29, CPU 2 under contest_limited.sh,
# doc/contest_reduction.pl's reduce_to_file/3 then decode_file/2, a fresh
# process each): weak_head and tabling(weak_head) read every problem
# correct, the sum of 64 digits in about 1.1 s of reduction. A reduced
# term written by hand as the canonical literal of the value reads wrong
# on the even zero and on the sum of 64 digits.
# These problems are no frontier: they check that a layer which plants
# values keeps to the terms its definitional code gives.
# LIMITS: the family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.

#
# Each text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes,
# imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. FIXME: the import projects "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
